00:51:16.000 --> 00:51:20.000
Mira: What did that move from traditional marketing automation to an Agentech system actually

00:51:20.000 --> 00:51:26.000
Mira: change in how you approached campaigns day to day?

00:51:26.000 --> 00:51:31.000
Piper: life cycle retention CRM marketer. And if any of your listeners are aware, it's a very,

00:51:31.000 --> 00:51:37.000
Piper: very tactical, very technical role in which you're building out logic systems and triggers

00:51:37.000 --> 00:51:44.000
Piper: as you input, you know, gather information about customers or subscribers or anyone sort

00:51:44.000 --> 00:51:48.000
Piper: of in your ecosystem of your product. You start gathering events, behavior and information

00:51:48.000 --> 00:51:53.000
Piper: and try to build out a series of touch points that could be a welcome email and

00:51:53.000 --> 00:51:56.000
Piper: someone first signs up for your email. It could be the follow-up push notifications

00:51:56.000 --> 00:52:02.000
Piper: you get after you sign up for a restaurant reservation. It could be the

00:52:02.000 --> 00:52:05.000
Piper: cart abandonment experience as you're shopping and you abandon your cart and

00:52:05.000 --> 00:52:09.000
Piper: you get a follow-up SMS or a ping. There's so many different ways and

00:52:09.000 --> 00:52:12.000
Piper: different channels, own channels that you can build out this customer

00:52:12.000 --> 00:52:15.000
Piper: engagement experience. And sometimes they're not always customers. Sometimes

00:52:15.000 --> 00:52:19.000
Piper: they're just simply users that you are trying to engage to have them be

00:52:19.000 --> 00:52:25.000
Piper: ready to purchase or ready to subscribe or upgrade from freemium to premium what have you just across

00:52:25.000 --> 00:52:30.000
Piper: channels and so much of my career was about building these logic systems mapping out customer

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:35.000
Piper: journeys understanding different touch points you know what's the common purchasing pattern over

00:52:35.000 --> 00:52:40.000
Piper: years that a customer takes with a certain type of organization what's their lifetime value

00:52:40.000 --> 00:52:43.000
Piper: and how do you kind of maximize these touch points to help nudge them along to help guide

00:52:43.000 --> 00:52:49.000
