00:54:24.000 --> 00:54:26.000
Piper: and at least in the past we did.

00:54:26.000 --> 00:54:27.000
Piper: We think about niches, we make assumptions

00:54:27.000 --> 00:54:29.000
Piper: about behaviors, we have to kind of have

00:54:29.000 --> 00:54:33.000
Piper: to stereotype about people's values and interests.

00:54:33.000 --> 00:54:35.000
Piper: And AMP thinks a little bit differently.

00:54:35.000 --> 00:54:39.000
Piper: AMP is basically providing this AI power

00:54:39.000 --> 00:54:42.000
Piper: and using a system of reinforcement learning

00:54:42.000 --> 00:54:45.000
Piper: to look at a one-to-one level,

00:54:45.000 --> 00:54:46.000
Piper: study each individual user,

00:54:46.000 --> 00:54:48.000
Piper: and then choose from sort of an approved library

00:54:48.000 --> 00:54:49.000
Piper: of content across channels

00:54:49.000 --> 00:54:51.000
Piper: and compose and put together messaging

00:54:51.000 --> 00:54:55.000
Piper: that it believes that person will most likely align with.

00:54:55.000 --> 00:54:56.000
Piper: It runs these micro experiments,

00:54:56.000 --> 00:54:59.000
Piper: these sort of one-to-one tests.

00:54:59.000 --> 00:55:01.000
Piper: It's more sophisticated than an A-B test

