Piper: only generate content but can actually help you decide if, when, and where someone's

00:55:45.000 --> 00:55:51.000
Piper: being contacted.

00:55:45.000 --> 00:55:51.000
Piper: So, it was a remarkable experience and it kind of opened my eyes to looking beyond AI as

00:55:51.000 --> 00:55:56.000
Piper: simply a generative tool, a support function for building out content.

00:55:56.000 --> 00:55:59.000
Piper: And I'll just say cannably, AMP has absolutely seen results.

00:55:59.000 --> 00:56:04.000
Piper: They were acquired by Mollengage just a few months ago and are now helping to work globally

00:56:04.000 --> 00:56:12.000
Piper: with massive enterprise and mid-market organizations to help them really identify, as some might

00:56:12.000 --> 00:56:16.000
Piper: say.

00:56:12.000 --> 00:56:16.000
Piper: but help them better improve their performance of all of their push

00:56:16.000 --> 00:56:20.000
Piper: notifications, their email, their SMS. And I will say one of the case studies we

00:56:20.000 --> 00:56:24.000
Piper: shared and one of the clients we worked on, in the first six months they were

00:56:24.000 --> 00:56:27.000
Piper: able to launch over a hundred of these agente campaigns, sort of equivalent to

00:56:27.000 --> 00:56:29.000
Piper: running a hundred automations, but again the automation is not triggered by a

00:56:29.000 --> 00:56:33.000
Piper: specific behavior. It's agents that are sort of choosing the triggers, choosing

00:56:33.000 --> 00:56:39.000
Piper: who gets what, and they launch over a hundred different sort of messaging

00:56:39.000 --> 00:56:44.000
Piper: experiences, at least sort of collections of messages and use cases that an agent could

00:56:44.000 --> 00:56:49.000
Piper: choose from. And users that were getting more personalized messages from these AI agents

00:56:49.000 --> 00:56:55.000
Piper: were indeed spending more time in app of this major sports media company, whose name

00:56:55.000 --> 00:57:08.000
Piper: I can't name, but a national sports association. And those users spent 13 and a half more

00:57:08.000 --> 00:57:13.000
Piper: the fact that people's needs and preferences change. We are all unique snowflakes. You get

00:57:13.000 --> 00:57:17.000
Piper: sick for two weeks. You get the flu and you're bed rotting and scrolling on your phone. Your

00:57:17.000 --> 00:57:21.000
Piper: behavior is inherently changing and certain agentic systems and AI decisioning systems

00:57:21.000 --> 00:57:24.000
Piper: are able to accommodate that and account for that and recognize a change in behavior

00:57:24.000 --> 00:57:28.000
Piper: mean that your preferences for content may have changed. They can run those micro experiences

00:57:28.000 --> 00:57:31.000
Piper: is at a one-to-one level, not in any way compromising

00:57:31.000 --> 00:57:35.000
Piper: or risking your greater audience for that type of engagement.

00:57:35.000 --> 00:57:39.000
Piper: So yeah, AI decisioning is truly fascinating.

00:57:39.000 --> 00:57:41.000
Piper: I think in five years, we're gonna see

00:57:41.000 --> 00:57:44.000
Piper: every major email, SMS, push notification tool,

00:57:44.000 --> 00:57:45.000
